{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-knot-centric-table-table3-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:knot-centric-table-table3-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 3 from rem:knot-centric-table","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-centric-table"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"knot-centric-table-table3-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:knot-centric-table-table3-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Data table 3 from rem:knot-centric-table</em></p>\n<p>Each nucleon-pair crossing carries a per-crossing weight in the skein-weighted contact form, split into a crossing weight coefficient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c</code> and a skein deformation term <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d \\propto q - q^{-1}</code>; the sign and magnitude of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d</code> encode the channel, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d = 0</code> giving the EM-repulsive proton pair and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d &#x3C; 0</code> the strong-attractive neutron pair.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Crossing</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d</code></th>\n<th>Physical</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}</code>-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{p}</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td>repulsive (EM)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n}</code>-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n}</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-(q - q^{-1})</code></td>\n<td>attractive (strong)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>mixed</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-\\frac{q - q^{-1}}{2}</code></td>\n<td>intermediate</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"}
